# ==============================================================================
# Environment Configuration Template (.env.example)
# Advaita Website: Supabase + Vercel + GitHub Complete Integration Guide
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. CLIENT-SAFE / PUBLIC SUPABASE CONFIGURATION (Exposed via Vite)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These values are public by design and embedded into the client bundle at build time.
# They are safely protected by database-level Row Level Security (RLS) policies.
# Find these in Supabase: Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development. Never commit `.env.local` to git!
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-public-anon-key

# Optional: Enable verbose Supabase debug logging in development console
# VITE_SUPABASE_DEBUG=false

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. VERCEL DEPLOYMENT CONFIGURATION (Settings -> Environment Variables)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# In your Vercel Project Dashboard:
# 1. Go to: Settings -> Environment Variables
# 2. Add the following variables (select Production, Preview, and Development):
#    - VITE_SUPABASE_URL = https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
#    - VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = your-public-anon-key
# 3. Optional keepalive authentication secret:
#    - CRON_SECRET = your-random-32-byte-secret-or-uuid
#
# NOTE: Vercel Cron automatically invokes `/api/keepalive` daily at 04:00 UTC
# to keep your Supabase PostgreSQL instance active and prevent inactivity sleep.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. GITHUB ACTIONS REPOSITORY SECRETS (Settings -> Secrets -> Actions)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# In your GitHub Repository:
# 1. Go to: Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions
# 2. Add the following Repository Secrets under "Secrets":
#    - VITE_SUPABASE_URL (or SUPABASE_URL) = https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
#    - VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY (or SUPABASE_ANON_KEY) = your-public-anon-key
#    - CRON_SECRET = your-random-32-byte-secret-or-uuid (matches Vercel)
#
# These allow GitHub Actions CI/CD to pre-render routes with live data and run
# automated keepalive database touches twice daily (04:00 and 16:00 UTC).

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. ZERO-LEAK SECURITY & PRECAUTIONS GUARANTEES
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# - NEVER prefix private secrets (like SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY) with `VITE_`.
# - NEVER commit `.env`, `.env.local`, or secret tokens to GitHub.
# - All database writes are enforced by Row-Level Security (RLS) on PostgreSQL.
# - Keepalive pings use `-s -o /dev/null` in CI to ensure zero token leakage in logs.